							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382968338645_407587_3038' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;In a development process items (parts or documents)&amp;#160;are often refined incrementally, so one &lt;i&gt;ItemVersion &lt;/i&gt;originates from another. The class &lt;i&gt;ItemHistoryEntry&lt;/i&gt; enables the description of predecessor / successor relationships between &lt;i&gt;ItemVersions&lt;/i&gt;. The description of both linear and branching relationships is possible. The relationship can be classified in order to distinguish between two cases:&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;ol&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The successor &lt;i&gt;ItemVersion&lt;/i&gt; is an instance of the same item (&lt;i&gt;type = &amp;quot;Sequence&amp;quot;&lt;/i&gt;)&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The successor &lt;i&gt;ItemVersion&lt;/i&gt; is an instance of a new but somehow similar item (&lt;i&gt;type = &amp;quot;derivation&amp;quot;&lt;/i&gt;).&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;    &lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382968260059_304148_2906'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382968655716_420421_3039' name='Item Equivalence' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382967898678_224517_2901'>
