							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_19_0_2_854026d_1622624045859_548001_5883' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The geometric properties of connector housings are closely related to the &lt;i&gt;LocalGeometrySpecification&lt;/i&gt;, described in the section &amp;quot;Coordinate Systems of Components&amp;quot;. Positions of common elements (e.g. &lt;i&gt;BoundingBox, PlacementPoint /&amp;#160;SegmentConnectionPoint&lt;/i&gt;) are defined in a &lt;i&gt;LocalGeometrySpecification.&lt;/i&gt; Within the &lt;i&gt;ConnectorHousingSpecification&lt;/i&gt; only those aspects that apply exclusively to connectors are defined. All definitions &amp;amp;&amp;#160;conventions that are required to define these geometric properties are described in the previous section.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;All geometric properties of a cavity within the context of a connector are aggregated in the&amp;#160;optional &lt;i&gt;CavityPositionDetail&lt;/i&gt;.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;&amp;#160;&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_19_0_2_854026d_1622624010804_359677_5870'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='_19_0_2_854026d_1637928127214_838340_6909' name='Wire Tupel' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382969329975_216295_3207'>
							<xmi:Extension extender='MagicDraw UML 2022x'>
