							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_2022x_1_854026d_1695907549928_76409_3659' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;&lt;i&gt;Height&lt;/i&gt; &amp;amp;&amp;#160;&lt;i&gt;Width&lt;/i&gt; of the crimp&lt;i&gt; &lt;/i&gt;are important quality criteria for the crimping process defined in the part master data of the terminal.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The core crimp and the insulation crimp have different heights &amp;amp;&amp;#160;width depending on multiple parameter cross-section, material, insulation thickness etc. Each &lt;i&gt;CrimpDetail&lt;/i&gt; represents a pair of &lt;i&gt;Height&lt;/i&gt; &amp;amp;&amp;#160;&lt;i&gt;Width &lt;/i&gt;(with optional &lt;i&gt;Tolerance)&lt;/i&gt; for specific parameter combination. &#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;Those parameters are not defined in the &lt;i&gt;CrimpDetail &lt;/i&gt;itself, but in the referenced &lt;i&gt;Conductor-&lt;/i&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;i&gt;InsulationSpecification.&lt;/i&gt; There are two possibilities here:&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;ol&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The &lt;i&gt;Conductor-&lt;/i&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;i&gt;InsulationSpecification&lt;/i&gt; can belong to the description of a specific wire. In this case, the specifications will most likely contain more information than the information required to determine the crimp parameters. &#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The &lt;i&gt;Conductor-&lt;/i&gt; &amp;amp; &lt;i&gt;InsulationSpecification&lt;/i&gt; can belong to the description of the terminal itself. In this case, the specifications represent a pattern for matching wires, by defining only the relevant attributes (e.g. &lt;i&gt;CrossSectionArea &amp;amp;&amp;#160;Material &lt;/i&gt;in the &lt;i&gt;ConductorSpecification&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;InsulationThickness &amp;amp;&amp;#160;Material&lt;/i&gt; in the &lt;i&gt;InsulationSpecification.&lt;/i&gt;  &#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;    &lt;/ol&gt;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_2022x_1_854026d_1695890860310_178337_2087'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='_2022x_1_854026d_1700127767818_601122_2063' name='Terminal Coordinate System' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382969329975_216295_3207'>
							<xmi:Extension extender='MagicDraw UML 2022x'>
								<diagramRepresentation>
									<diagram:DiagramRepresentationObject ID='_2022x_1_854026d_1700127767831_218173_2068' initialFrameSizeSet='true' requiredFeature=';UML_Standard_Profile.mdzip^UML_FEATURE~~' type='Class Diagram' umlType='Class Diagram' xmi:id='_gD-5gIRkEe6EMLitfrrNAQ' xmi:version='2.0' xmlns:binary='http://www.nomagic.com/ns/cameo/client/binary/1.0' xmlns:diagram='http://www.nomagic.com/ns/magicdraw/core/diagram/1.0' xmlns:xmi='http://www.omg.org/XMI' xmlns:xsi='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance'>
										<diagramContents contentHash='7b39fabba898fe707fcdd145eb0ef794c4699199' exporterName='MagicDraw UML' exporterVersion='2022x v7' xmi:id='_gD-5gYRkEe6EMLitfrrNAQ'>
											<binaryObject streamContentID='BINARY-646bb812-b7fa-4a2d-9937-5b84886e48b1' xmi:id='_gD-5goRkEe6EMLitfrrNAQ' xsi:type='binary:StreamIdentityBinaryObject'/>
										</diagramContents>
									</diagram:DiagramRepresentationObject>
								</diagramRepresentation>
							</xmi:Extension>
							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_2022x_1_854026d_1700133036070_542098_2118' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The coordinate system of a terminal defines a reference system for the definition of other values (e.g. the &lt;i&gt;WireReception.Rotation&lt;/i&gt;). The definition is the following&amp;#160;(see illustration).&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;ol&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The origin (0,0,0)&amp;#160;is in the intersection point the centerline of terminal (z-axis) and the perpendicular plane through the most forward end position of the terminal in its cavity.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The y-axis points in the direction of the primary locking.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The x-axis is the cross product of y and z, x&amp;#160;=&amp;#160;y ⨯ z).&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;    &lt;/ol&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The rotation of the &lt;i&gt;WireReception&lt;/i&gt; is the angle between the normal vector on base plane of the crimp area and the y-axis, which is a rotation around the z-axis (right hand rule, compare illustration). &#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;&amp;#160;&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_2022x_1_854026d_1700127767818_601122_2063'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='_2022x_1_854026d_1734679322918_868507_2350' name='Fixings Coordinates and Dimensions' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382969329975_216295_3207'>
							<xmi:Extension extender='MagicDraw UML 2022x'>
								<diagramRepresentation>
									<diagram:DiagramRepresentationObject ID='_2022x_1_854026d_1734679322927_416115_2355' initialFrameSizeSet='true' requiredFeature=';UML_Standard_Profile.mdzip^UML_FEATURE~~' type='Class Diagram' umlType='Class Diagram' xmi:id='_G-2jAL6jEe-3f9Z54eVz8Q' xmi:version='2.0' xmlns:binary='http://www.nomagic.com/ns/cameo/client/binary/1.0' xmlns:diagram='http://www.nomagic.com/ns/magicdraw/core/diagram/1.0' xmlns:xmi='http://www.omg.org/XMI' xmlns:xsi='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance'>
										<diagramContents contentHash='86645bda3db32c30b6a04aa2c7ad441861e1098f' exporterName='MagicDraw UML' exporterVersion='2022x v7' xmi:id='_G-2jAb6jEe-3f9Z54eVz8Q'>
											<binaryObject streamContentID='BINARY-0302bc31-6fe7-462a-9d0d-e1a147773795' xmi:id='_G-2jAr6jEe-3f9Z54eVz8Q' xsi:type='binary:StreamIdentityBinaryObject'/>
										</diagramContents>
									</diagram:DiagramRepresentationObject>
								</diagramRepresentation>
							</xmi:Extension>
							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_2022x_1_854026d_1734679803511_614875_2371' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The following section contains specifications for the definition of coordinate systems of fixings, clips, cable ties and similar (and their 3D models). These coordinate definitions form the basis for various attribute definitions and the placement of components on the wire harness (see &lt;i&gt;PlacementSpecification&lt;/i&gt;) and in the 3D model (see BuildingBlockSpecification3D) . For components whose geometry changes upon installation, the installed state must be used. &#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The orientation of the coordinate system of cable ties shall be as follows:&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;ul&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The origin of the cable tie lies centrally at the edge of the lock on the side of the cable tie.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The Y-axis is positioned in the plane of the wire harness support surface and is oriented parallel to the direction in which the wire harness passes through the cable tie.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The XZ plane intersects the wire harness.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;For fixings with cable tie (including those with attached cable ties), only the fastening is represented. The cable tie itself (which varies in diameter) and its closure are omitted. &#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The orientation of the coordinate system of fixings shall be as follows:&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;ul&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The origin of the component lies at the intersection of the support surface of the fixing (in the installed state) with the central axis of the locking pin, bolt holder, or hole/slot (depending on the fastening method).&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The Y-axis is in the plane of the support surface and oriented parallel to the direction in which the cable harness passes through the fixing.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The Z-axis is perpendicular to the plane of the support surface and points in the opposite direction to the clip&#39;s mounting direction.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;    &lt;/ul&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;For fastening elements attached to an edge, the origin of the component is located at the intersection of the support surface of the component (in the installed state) with the center of the side contact surface of the component on the sheet metal.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;If the conditions described above cannot be met, the following priorities should be applied:&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;ol&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The Y-axis is oriented parallel to the direction in which the cable harness passes through the fixing and lies in the plane of a support or contact surface.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The XZ plane must intersect the cable at the point where the position of the component on the segment is dimensioned (e.g., in the middle of the cable tie for cable tie holders).&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;      &lt;li&gt;&#10;The YZ plane lies in the middle of the component.&#10;&#10;      &lt;/li&gt;&#10;    &lt;/ol&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;Definitions were adopted from the CES&amp;#160;guidelines.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;&amp;#160;&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_2022x_1_854026d_1734679322918_868507_2350'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='_2022x_1_854026d_1749713582218_850900_1730' name='Modular Connector Housings' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382969329975_216295_3207'>
							<xmi:Extension extender='MagicDraw UML 2022x'>
								<diagramRepresentation>
									<diagram:DiagramRepresentationObject ID='_2022x_1_854026d_1749713582227_3575_1735' initialFrameSizeSet='true' requiredFeature=';UML_Standard_Profile.mdzip^UML_FEATURE~~' type='Class Diagram' umlType='Class Diagram' xmi:id='_eMcuMEdfEfCmIuz55VbOYA' xmi:version='2.0' xmlns:binary='http://www.nomagic.com/ns/cameo/client/binary/1.0' xmlns:diagram='http://www.nomagic.com/ns/magicdraw/core/diagram/1.0' xmlns:xmi='http://www.omg.org/XMI' xmlns:xsi='http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance'>
										<diagramContents contentHash='79c04bafcc8439923f4f58c4e4266e3a0ac455ca' exporterName='MagicDraw UML' exporterVersion='2022x v7' xmi:id='_eMcuMUdfEfCmIuz55VbOYA'>
											<binaryObject streamContentID='BINARY-9e075d2d-7f05-4cab-9146-b48b384eceb9' xmi:id='_eMcuMkdfEfCmIuz55VbOYA' xsi:type='binary:StreamIdentityBinaryObject'/>
											<usedObjects href='PROJECT-195e27c6-e36a-4b96-9301-e34bebde338f?resource=com.nomagic.magicdraw.uml_umodel.shared_umodel#EAID_F81D9D7E_52AA_41a9_9133_E16D3AE25095'/>
											<usedObjects href='PROJECT-195e27c6-e36a-4b96-9301-e34bebde338f?resource=com.nomagic.magicdraw.uml_umodel.shared_umodel#_2022x_1_854026d_1749725287875_735843_2379'/>
											<usedObjects href='PROJECT-195e27c6-e36a-4b96-9301-e34bebde338f?resource=com.nomagic.magicdraw.uml_umodel.shared_umodel#_2022x_1_854026d_1749714841863_316741_2146'/>
											<usedObjects href='PROJECT-195e27c6-e36a-4b96-9301-e34bebde338f?resource=com.nomagic.magicdraw.uml_umodel.shared_umodel#_17_0_2_4_854026d_1443699802034_874606_2681'/>
