							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_19_0_2_854026d_1573047294298_675484_5454' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;A &lt;i&gt;TopologyZoneSpecification&lt;/i&gt; is a container to define &lt;i&gt;TopologyZones.&lt;/i&gt; A &lt;i&gt;TopologyZone&lt;/i&gt; is a way to define areas on that share a set of properties (e.g. environmental influence).&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;To define the &lt;i&gt;TopologyZone &lt;/i&gt;unambiguously an assignment of the topology elements to their zones is necessary. &lt;i&gt;TopologyNodes&lt;/i&gt; are only connecting points for &lt;i&gt;TopologySegments&lt;/i&gt; or for the placement of components and do not have any own extent in space. Therefore, &lt;i&gt;ZoneAssignments &lt;/i&gt;are only possible for &lt;i&gt;T&lt;/i&gt;&lt;i&gt;opologySegments&lt;/i&gt;.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;For more details, see the description of the relevant classes.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_18_5_2_854026d_1542703592071_369943_6158'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
