							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_19_0_2_854026d_1637938783592_39328_7355' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;A &lt;i&gt;Specification&lt;/i&gt; to define requirements for the handling of wire / wire element tuples (pairs, triple,...) with the focus on twisting&amp;#160;/&amp;#160;untwisting. The &lt;i&gt;WireTupleSpecification&lt;/i&gt; defines the technical properties of the untwisting from a part master data perspective&amp;#160;(see also the diagram &amp;quot;Wire&amp;#160;Tupel&amp;quot;&amp;#160;in &amp;quot;Component&amp;#160;Characteristics&amp;quot;). The &lt;i&gt;WireTupleTermination&lt;/i&gt; defines properties for a specific end of a specific wire tupel (a concrete usage).&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;&amp;#160;&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_19_0_2_854026d_1637932593831_372159_7053'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
