							<ownedComment xmi:type='uml:Comment' xmi:id='_17_0_2_4_854026d_1382964519538_715817_2451' body='&lt;html&gt;&#10;  &lt;head&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;style&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;p {padding:0px; margin:0px;}&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/style&gt;&#10;&#9;&lt;/head&gt;&#10;  &lt;body&gt;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;The VEC provides a concept for the localization of string values. Every attribute that can be localized has the type of &lt;i&gt;AbstractLocalizedString&lt;/i&gt; or one of its subclasses.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;An &lt;i&gt;AbstractLocalizedString&lt;/i&gt; consists of an ISO &lt;i&gt;languageCode&lt;/i&gt; and a &lt;i&gt;value&lt;/i&gt;. Attributes of this type have a multiplicity of [0..*].&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;In the case of a &lt;i&gt;LocalizedString&lt;/i&gt; the attribute represents a human readable text with a specific semantic. All &lt;i&gt;LocalizedString&lt;/i&gt; instances for a single attribute must represent the same meaning in different languages.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;    &lt;p&gt;&#10;When a &lt;i&gt;LocalizedTypedString &lt;/i&gt;is used,&lt;i&gt; &lt;/i&gt;the semantics of the attribute values can be further detailed by the &lt;i&gt;type&lt;/i&gt; attribute. For example, an &lt;i&gt;ItemVersion&lt;/i&gt; can have more than one description with a more specific semantic of each description type. In this case, all &lt;i&gt;LocalizedTypedString&lt;/i&gt; instances for an attribute must represent the same meaning for their type value in different languages.&#10;&#10;    &lt;/p&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;/body&gt;&#10;&lt;/html&gt;'>
								<annotatedElement xmi:idref='_17_0_2_854026d_1382704093009_266599_2360'/>
							</ownedComment>
						</ownedDiagram>
						<ownedDiagram xmi:type='uml:Diagram' xmi:id='EAID_5D1D8F3B_5260_4a3c_AC3F_0A1B5B0F5B94' name='Extensibility with Custom Properties' visibility='public' ownerOfDiagram='_19_0_2_854026d_1576576624840_362630_6255'>
